<p>
    <strong>Core Gameplan:</strong> Goblins comes at you from two directions:
    fast early beats plus card advantage from the back end (<a
        role="button" tabindex="0"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Goblin Ringleader">Goblin Ringleader</a
    >, <a
        role="button" tabindex="0"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Siege-Gang Commander"
        >Siege-Gang Commander</a
    >). Leaning on early <a
        role="button" tabindex="0"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Meddling Mage">Meddling Mage</a
    > is risky here—Mage can't profitably block a Turn 1 <a
        role="button" tabindex="0"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Goblin Lackey">Goblin Lackey</a
    > on the draw, and it can't block pro-blue beaters like
    <a
        role="button" tabindex="0"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Goblin Piledriver">Goblin Piledriver</a
    > at all. If you survive the first three turns, you win.
</p>
<p>
    <strong>Sideboard Strategy:</strong> Cut all your <a
        role="button" tabindex="0"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Meddling Mage">Meddling Mage</a
    > and slow enchantment removal like <a
        role="button" tabindex="0"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Seal of Cleansing">Seal of Cleansing</a
    >. Bring in your fourth <a
        role="button" tabindex="0"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Swords to Plowshares"
        >Swords to Plowshares</a
    >, <a
        role="button" tabindex="0"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Hydroblast">Hydroblast</a
    >, <a
        role="button" tabindex="0"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Exalted Angel">Exalted Angel</a
    >, and extra <a
        role="button" tabindex="0"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Tsabo's Web">Tsabo's Web</a
    > to shut down their <a
        role="button" tabindex="0"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Rishadan Port">Rishadan Port</a
    >. Killing a Turn 1 <a
        role="button" tabindex="0"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Goblin Lackey">Goblin Lackey</a
    > before it can connect is the most important thing you can do.
</p>
